the  scrub  upon  completion.  Scrubbing and resilvering are very
similar operations. The difference is that resilvering only exam‐
ines data that knows to be out of date (for example, when attach‐
ing a new device to a mirror or replacing  an  existing  device),
whereas scrubbing examines all data to discover silent errors due
to hardware faults or disk failure.  Because scrubbing and resil‐
vering  are  operations, only allows one at a time. If a scrub is
already in progress, the command returns an error. To start a new
scrub, you have to stop the old scrub with the command first.  If
a  resilver  is in progress, does not allow a scrub to be started
until the resilver completes.  Stop scrubbing.   Sets  the  given
